From ad78325a586981d9e9b80673958e8d723a32eab0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gregory R. Lee" <grelee@nvidia.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 07:57:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Report samples replaced by safe overflow

Add an optional publisher callback for each unread sample replaced by a
safe-overflow send. Report the service, publisher, and affected
subscriber identifiers together with borrowed views of the replaced
sample's user header and payload before its reference is released.

Expose the callback consistently through the Rust, C FFI, and C++
publisher builders so applications can attribute data loss to an exact
receiver instead of observing only an aggregate delivery count.

Upstream-Status: Pending [upstream submission not yet prepared]

